  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "isolated red, green, and teal marker pixels on black background",
  "transform": "keep each marker; paint the centered 3x3 hollow outline around green in pink, teal in yellow, and red in blue"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 6-16 rows x 6-16 cols, black background, input == output size
  markers:
    count: 1-3 single-pixel markers on black background
    colors: subset of {red, green, teal}; each color appears at most once [observed]
    placement: each marker at least 1 cell from every grid edge (row/col in [1, H-2]/[1, W-2])
    separation: Chebyshev distance >= 3 between any two markers (so 3x3 outlines never overlap)
  transform:
    rule: keep each marker pixel; paint its 8 surrounding cells with paired outline color
    color_map: green->pink, teal->yellow, red->blue
    geometry: 3x3 hollow square centered on marker (center unchanged, 8 border cells filled)
    all 8 outline cells must be black in input (no overlap with other markers or outlines)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct placement (constraints are simple enough for forward generation)
  steps:
    1. pick grid size H, W each uniformly from 6-16
    2. pick marker count N from 1-3
    3. pick N distinct colors from {red, green, teal}
    4. place markers one at a time at random positions in [1, H-2] x [1, W-2]
    5. reject/retry a position if its 3x3 neighborhood overlaps any previously placed marker's 3x3 neighborhood (Chebyshev distance < 3 between centers)
    6. grid is all black except the N marker pixels
```
